      en: "The Ramena Battery is a late 19th-century coastal artillery fortification built by the French colonial administration to protect the port of Diego-Suarez (now Antsiranana). Perched on a rocky headland, it commanded the entrance to the bay. The battery featured several gun emplacements, ammunition magazines, and barracks, all constructed from local stone. During World War II, it was manned by Vichy French forces until captured by Allied troops in 1942. Today, the site is a popular tourist attraction, offering panoramic views of the Indian Ocean and the surrounding landscape. The ruins are a testament to Madagascar's colonial military history.",
